#%PAM-1.0
# PAM service of the rynas web interface, used by rynasd (root) to check passwords.
# Install as /etc/pam.d/rynas. Without this file rynasd falls back to the "login" service.
#
# Only auth and account are used: rynas opens no PAM session (no pam_systemd, no
# pam_mkhomedir), so a web login does not start a user session.
# Who may log in is decided by rynas itself (groups rynas-admin or sudo by default),
# pam_unix's failure delay and rynas' own rate limiting slow down guessing.

@include common-auth
@include common-account
